se, billed monthly | | Annual (364 nights) | $3,750 + metered electric | Metered — you pay for what you use, billed monthly | | DISCOUNTS | Weekly (7) = $31.43/day ( Save $4.57/day ) | Monthly (30) = $12.50/day ( Save $23.50/day ) | Yearly (364) = $10.30/day ( Save $25.70/day. Annual site: $3,750. That’s $750 off – 2 months free vs. paying monthly. Ca", "| Metered — you pay for what you use, billed monthly | | DISCOUNTS | Weekly (7) = $31.43/day ( Save $4.57/day ) | Monthly (30) = $12.50/day ( Save $23.50/day ) | Yearly (364) = $10.30/day ( Save $25.70/day. Annual site: $3,750. That’s $750 off – 2 months free vs. paying monthly. Cancellations require 3 business days’ notice. ) | Straight A’s Discount — 5% Off | Kids hitting the books? Families with a child enrolled i"], "via": "Prices / Rental Info"}, {"url": "https://mountainhomervpark.com/terms-and-conditions-rv-park-rules/", "lines": ["re on premises next door to our offices. | PAYMENTS & DUE DATES | Payment for a reservation is due at time of booking if online, or at time of check-in if paying in person. | Here is our site fee breakdown: | Daily Rate $36/night + taxes (electricity included). Weekly Rate $220/week (7 nights) + taxes (electricity included). Monthly Rate $375/month (30 nights) + metered electric. Annual Rate $3,750/year (364 nights) ", " online, or at time of check-in if paying in person. | Here is our site fee breakdown: | Daily Rate $36/night + taxes (electricity included). Weekly Rate $220/week (7 nights) + taxes (electricity included). Monthly Rate $375/month (30 nights) + metered electric. Annual Rate $3,750/year (364 nights) + metered electric. That’s $750 off — 2 months free vs. paying monthly. Paid in full for 1 year, non-refundable. | Per-d", "$375/month (30 nights) + metered electric. Annual Rate $3,750/year (364 nights) + metered electric. That’s $750 off — 2 months free vs. paying monthly. Paid in full for 1 year, non-refundable. | Per-day breakdown: Daily $36/day. Weekly $31.43/day. Monthly $12.50/day (+ metered electricity). Annual $10.30/day (+ metered electricity). | A refundable damage deposit of $100 is due at move-in for monthly and annual stays.", "ly. Paid in full for 1 year, non-refundable. | Per-day breakdown: Daily $36/day. Weekly $31.43/day. Monthly $12.50/day (+ metered electricity). Annual $10.30/day (+ metered electricity). | A refundable damage deposit of $100 is due at move-in for monthly and annual stays. The deposit is refunded once site fee and electric charges are paid in full and the site is left in good condition, ordinary wear and tear excepted", "ess days’ notice. | No-shows, or cancellations without written notice to us, forfeit 100% of the reservation. | Late arrivals may still use the remainder of their reservation, but there is no refund for days missed. | A $25 late fee applies to any site fee payment not received within 5 days of the due date. | A 3% surcharge applies to site fee payments made by credit card. | ACH / direct deposits are accepted with no", "yment confirmation must be received by the due date. | Military families: 5% off, always. | Straight A’s students: 5% off, always. | Occupancy & Guests | The base rate covers 2 adults per site. | Additional adult (18+): $2/day. Additional child (under 18): $1/day. | You are responsible for your children and their conduct. Keep them supervised, courteous to other guests, and out of other guests’ sites. | Your Lot | Ke", "similar additions may not exceed 8 feet wide by 16 feet long, and must be professionally built on 4″ x 6″ beams. | Keep your RV and lot in good, safe condition. | Water leaks: if your water hose connection is leaking, a $20 fine will be added to your account for each day until it is fixed. Water is included in the site fee — fixing leaks promptly keeps it that way. | Pets | Pets must be leashed while on the grounds, "], "via": "Park Rules & Terms"}, {"url": "https://mountainhomervpark.com/rv-sewer-dump-station-mountain-home-ar/", "lines": ["RV Dump Station in Mountain Home, AR | $25 Sewer Dump Prices / Rental Info WiFi Setup Info | Park Rules & Terms | | Services RV Dump Station | EV Charging | | Why Choose Us? Laundry Facilities | Military Discount | | Local Attractions | Bo", "r hose to our sewer connection, dump your tanks. Our sewer hookups are the same full-size connections our monthly guests use — not some trickling dump pad. Most rigs are done in 15 minutes. | Dump Pricing | Sewer dump — $25. Hook into our sewer line and empty your black and gray tanks. No site booking needed, no overnight stay required — just call ahead to confirm. | Fresh-water spray-down — add $10. Hook into our wa", "5 minutes. | Dump Pricing | Sewer dump — $25. Hook into our sewer line and empty your black and gray tanks. No site booking needed, no overnight stay required — just call ahead to confirm. | Fresh-water spray-down — add $10. Hook into our water spigot to rinse and spray down after you dump. A clean finish for ten bucks. | Call ahead to confirm availability, then check in at the office during office hours and we’ll po", "the spray-down rinse, bring a dedicated rinse hose (keep it separate from your drinking-water hose). | Charging Your EV While You’re Here | Driving electric too? Top off your car at our 50-amp pedestals while you dump — $20 plus metered electricity, no site booking needed. Call ahead to confirm. | See our EV charging services | Dump Station FAQ | Where can I dump my RV tanks near Mountain Home, AR? | Right here. Moun", "head to confirm. | See our EV charging services | Dump Station FAQ | Where can I dump my RV tanks near Mountain Home, AR? | Right here. Mountain Home RV Park at 628 County Road 390 offers drive-in sewer dump service for $25 — no booking or overnight stay required. Call ahead to confirm before driving in. | How much does it cost to dump RV black water tanks? | Our sewer dump is $25. Add a fresh-water spray-down rinse ", " 628 County Road 390 offers drive-in sewer dump service for $25 — no booking or overnight stay required. Call ahead to confirm before driving in. | How much does it cost to dump RV black water tanks? | Our sewer dump is $25. Add a fresh-water spray-down rinse for $10 more. | Do I need to stay overnight to use your dump station? | No. Drive-in dump service is open to everyone — no site booking needed. Just call (870) ", ". | Can big rigs use your dump? | Yes. Our sewer connections are full-size site hookups with room to maneuver. If you can drive it here, you can dump it here. | Is water available to rinse after dumping? | Yes — add the $10 spray-down and hook into our water spigot to rinse down. Bring your own rinse hose. | Do you offer dump service for non-guests? | That’s exactly what this is. Our $25 drive-in dump service is open", "er available to rinse after dumping? | Yes — add the $10 spray-down and hook into our water spigot to rinse down. Bring your own rinse hose. | Do you offer dump service for non-guests? | That’s exactly what this is. Our $25 drive-in dump service is open to anyone passing through, guest or not — call ahead to confirm. | Ready to Dump? | Call (870) 499-1608 Office, Laundry, Gift Shop | CHECK IN / OUT | CHECK IN BY 2PM,"], "via": "RV Dump Station"}, {"url": "https://mountainhomervpark.com/long-term-rv-park-mountain-home-arkansas/", "lines": ["Long-Term RV Park Mountain Home Arkansas | $375/Month Sites Prices / Rental Info WiFi Setup Info | Park Rules & Terms | | Services RV Dump Station | EV Charging | | Why Choose Us? Laundry Facilities | Military Discount | | Local Attractions | ", "es & Terms | | Services RV Dump Station | EV Charging | | Why Choose Us? Laundry Facilities | Military Discount | | Local Attractions | Book Now | Contact & Visit | Login | Long-Term RV Park in Mountain Home, Arkansas — $375/Month | If you need a place to park your rig for a month, a season, or a year — and you want it cheap, honest, and in a real town — you’re reading the right page. | Mountain Home RV Park by Jimos", "amilies between houses — building, buying, or waiting on a closing date. The kids stay in the same school. Nobody lives in a motel. | Retirees who sold the house and never looked back. Fixed income goes a lot further at $375 a month. | Anglers who fish the White River and the Twin Lakes all season. Park the rig for three months for less than a week at a lodge costs. | If that sounds like you, you’ll fit in fine. | Ra", "ver and the Twin Lakes all season. Park the rig for three months for less than a week at a lodge costs. | If that sounds like you, you’ll fit in fine. | Rates — straight numbers, no games | Stay Price Electric | Daily | $36/night + taxes | Included | | Weekly | $220 for 7 nights + taxes | Included | | Monthly | $375 for 30 nights | Metered — you pay for what you use | | Annual | $3,750 | Metered — $750 off, 2 months ", "traight numbers, no games | Stay Price Electric | Daily | $36/night + taxes | Included | | Weekly | $220 for 7 nights + taxes | Included | | Monthly | $375 for 30 nights | Metered — you pay for what you use | | Annual | $3,750 | Metered — $750 off, 2 months free vs. paying monthly | | Active and retired military take 5% off. Always. | No resort fees. No amenity fees. No surprise charges at checkout. The price on this", "e here. | Laundry on site | Dog park | Trash service | Office and gift shop with the basics | Pets welcome — clean up after them | Why monthly beats renting an apartment | A typical 2-bedroom around here rents for about $790 a month. Our monthly site is $375 plus metered electric. Most folks save a few hundred bucks a month, live 10 minutes from Lake Norfork, and walk to groceries and hardware in town. | And when the", " 2 PM, checkout by 11 AM. Cancellations need 3 business days’ notice. We’re usually in the office by 10 AM, and we take reservation calls 24 hours a day — if we’re not here, call and we’ll meet you shortly. | The deal | $375 a month. Full hookups. Fast internet. In town. Near the best fishing in Arkansas. | Call 870-499-1608 or email info@mountainhomervpark.com . Tell us when you’re coming. We’ll save you a pad. | Re"], "via": "Long-Term RV Stays"}]}
